              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that Congress enacted 18\u202fU.S.C.\u202f1956(h) solely to increase penalties for money\u2011laundering conspiracies."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners contend that the venue provision in 18\u202fU.S.C.\u202f1956(i) is the exclusive venue provision for money\u2011laundering offenses."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that, because before the enactment of \u00a7\u202f1956(h) the government had to prosecute money\u2011laundering conspiracies under \u00a7\u202f371 for six years, Congress intended to carry forward the overt\u2011act requirement of \u00a7\u202f371 into the money\u2011laundering conspiracy offense."
      }
    ],
