                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, congress enacted 18\u202fU.S.C.\u202f1956(h) for the sole purpose of increasing the penalties for money\u2011laundering conspiracies."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, the venue provision in 18\u202fU.S.C.\u202f1956(i) is the exclusive venue provision for money\u2011laundering."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 29,
                "start": 29
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, because before \u00a7\u202f1956(h) the government had to prosecute money\u2011laundering conspiracies under \u00a7\u202f371 for six years, the Court should presume that Congress intended to perpetuate the overt\u2011act requirement of \u00a7\u202f371 into the money\u2011laundering conspiracy offense."
